:: place.kim-office
  @hub home_kim
  Kim is sitting at {{npc.kim.dependent}} desk. {{npc.kim.subject | cap}} looks up as you enter.

  @if story.quest.rent.active and story.quest.rent.debt > 0
    Kim's ledger shows £{{story.quest.rent.debt}} in outstanding rent.

  @elseif story.quest.rent.debt > 0
    It looks like you've paid off your rent... for now.
  @endif

  @choicegroup ""
    @choice "Ask about the rent" -> story.rent.intro.2
      @when flags.quest.rent.intro_2 and not flags.quest.rent.intro_bypassed
    @endchoice

    @choice "Pay £200 toward rent" -> story.rent.payment
      @when story.quest.rent.active and story.quest.rent.debt >= 200 and player.money >= 200
      @change money -200 "£200 rent payment"
      @effect add story.quest.rent.debt -200
    @endchoice
  @endchoicegroup

:: story.rent.landlord-visit -> story.rent.intro.2
  @pool interrupt
  @when flags.home.opening_seen
  @when time.day > 2 or (time.day == 2 and time.minutesSinceMidnight >= 960)
  @when not story.quest.rent.active
  @when not flags.quest.rent.landlord_visit_seen
  @priority 200
  @choices "There is no more putting this off"
  @onenter
    @effect set local.at_office place.key == "home_kim"
    @effect set local.had_office_address flags.quest.rent.intro_2 == true
    @effect set local.contacted_kim flags.quest.rent.home_notice_resolved == true
    @effect set local.read_notice flags.quest.rent.home_notice_read == true
    @effect set flags.quest.rent.landlord_visit_seen
    @effect set flags.quest.rent.intro_bypassed
    @effect unset flags.quest.rent.intro_2
    @effect reminder clear home_rent_notice_1
    @effect chat finish kim.rent
    @effect unlock place home_kim
    @effect teleport npc kim player
  @endonenter

  @passage found

  @if local.at_office
    Before you can turn around or pretend you came for some other reason, Kim rises from behind {{npc.kim.dependent}} desk and closes the office door.
  @elseif place.key == "player_home"
    A firm knock rattles your front door. When you open it, a neatly dressed woman is waiting in the hall with a folder tucked beneath one arm.
  @elseif place.id
    A neatly dressed woman steps inside and calls your name. She spots you before you have time to wonder how she found you.
  @else
    A neatly dressed woman calls your name from behind you. She is carrying a folder and wearing the expression of someone who has already run out of patience.
  @endif

  "I'm Kim Johnson, your landlord. We need to discuss the account for {{home.location.name}}."

  @if local.at_office
    "You are here about the rent," Kim says. "Sit down. We are settling the account now."
  @elseif local.had_office_address
    "I gave you my office address. Since you haven't come to see me, I've come to collect you instead."
  @elseif local.contacted_kim
    "This has gone far enough by message. You're coming to my office so that we can settle it properly."
  @elseif local.read_notice
    "You saw the notice, but you never followed it up. I'm not leaving the account unresolved."
  @else
    "A notice was left on your door this afternoon. You haven't even looked at it, so I'm handling this in person."
  @endif

  @if local.at_office
    Kim points to the chair across from {{npc.kim.dependent}} desk. The invitation does not sound optional.
  @else
    Kim does not make the request sound optional. A few minutes later, you are on your way to {{npc.kim.home.location.name}} with {{npc.kim.object}}.
  @endif

  @choice "Sit down with Kim" -> story.rent.intro.2
    @when local.at_office
    @effect teleport npc kim home
  @endchoice

  @choice "Go with Kim" -> story.rent.intro.2
    @when not local.at_office
    @effect teleport npc kim home
    @effect relocate nearest-place home_kim
  @endchoice

:: story.rent.intro.2 -> @exit
  @onenter
    @effect set story.quest.rent.active true
    @effect set story.quest.rent.debt 800
    @effect set story.quest.rent_charges_issued 0
    @effect reminder clear home_rent_notice_1
    @effect reminder add rent_due
    @effect teleport npc kim home
  @endonenter

  @passage account

  @if flags.quest.rent.intro_bypassed
    Kim leads you into a cramped office and closes the door. Stacks of paper crowd {{npc.kim.dependent}} desk, and the light from a computer monitor flickers across rows of carefully labelled files.

    "Now that I finally have your attention, we can deal with this properly." Kim sits down and turns a lease toward you. "The account for {{home.location.name}} starts with two missed monthly payments: £800. I collect payments in £200 weekly instalments."
  @else
    You look around the office. Stacks of paper crowd Kim's desk, and the light from a computer monitor flickers across the files. Kim is sitting in a chair behind the desk, {{@if npc.kim.gender == "female"}}wearing a smart business suit and glasses{{@else}}wearing an ironed white shirt and glasses{{@endif}}. {{npc.kim.dependent | cap}} eyes are brown, and they follow you as you open your mouth to speak.

    "Hello. You must be from {{home.location.name}}, yes?" Kim turns the lease toward you. "The account starts with the two missed monthly payments: £800. I collect payments in £200 weekly instalments."
  @endif

  @choice "Try to explain" -> .explain
  @endchoice

  @choice "\"I don't have £800\"" -> .no-money
  @endchoice

  @choice "Pay (800£)" -> .pay
    @when player.money >= 800
    @change money -800
    @effect add story.quest.rent.debt -800
  @endchoice

  @passage explain

  @if flags.quest.rent.intro_bypassed
    "There has to be some mistake," you say. You try not to be intimidated by the way Kim is sitting completely straight. "I've only just moved here. I haven't even had a chance to pay rent yet."
  @else
    "As I said in my message, this must be some mistake," you begin. You try not to be intimidated by the way Kim is sitting completely straight. "I've only moved here very recently, and I haven't even had a chance to pay rent yet. I don't know how this could have happened."
  @endif

  Kim's expression doesn't change. "I don't make mistakes," {{npc.kim.subject}} says. "I keep a thorough record of *all* my tenants. The property at {{home.location.name}} has been registered for two months, and I am not in the business of charity." @change stat stress 5

  @choice "\"I don't have £800\"" -> .no-money
  @endchoice

  @choice "Pay (800£)" -> .pay
    @when player.money >= 800
    @change money -800
    @effect add story.quest.rent.debt -800
  @endchoice

  @passage no-money

  @if player.money < 800
    "I don't have the money to pay you right now," you say, trying to keep your voice calm. "Is there any way I can work something out with you?"
  @else
    "This seems steep," you say, trying to keep your voice calm. "Is there any way I can work something out with you?"
  @endif

  Kim folds {{npc.kim.dependent}} hands over the ledger. "Then pay what you can each week. Leaving it unpaid will only make the account worse."
  There's an uncomfortable emphasis on the word "worse" as {{npc.kim.subject}} says this. @change stat stress 8

  @next -> .leave

  @passage pay

  You hand over the 800£ to Kim. {{npc.kim.subject | cap}} takes it and puts it in a drawer.

  "Perfect!" {{npc.kim.subject}} says. "You are all caught up on your rent. Please make sure to pay on time in the future."  @change stat stress 5

  There's a note of self satisfaction in {{npc.kim.dependent}} voice as {{npc.kim.subject}} says this.

  @next

  "Now, was there something else?" Kim looks at you expectantly. {{npc.kim.dependent | cap}} teeth are very white as {{npc.kim.subject}} smiles widely.

  @choice "Leave" -> .leave
  @endchoice

  @choice "Flatter {{npc.kim.object}}?" -> .flirt
    @hint relationship kim.affection 5 "+Affection?"
  @endchoice

  @passage flirt

  "Oh what big teeth you have!" you joke, grinning at {{npc.kim.object}}. Immediately, Kim's smile falters, and {{npc.kim.subject}} looks at you with a mixture of confusion and concern.
  "What are you talking about?" {{npc.kim.subject}} asks, frowning. "That's not very flattering." @change relationship kim.intimidation 10

  {{npc.kim.subject | cap}} keeps looking straight at you, unsmiling this time. You avert your eyes.

  @next "Just leave" -> .leave

  @passage leave

  @effect unset flags.quest.rent.intro_2
  @effect teleport npc kim home
  @effect timer start rent.weekly

  You leave the office with a copy of the account. {{@if story.quest.rent.debt >= 800}}The £800 balance is overdue, and {{@else}}You have paid the outstanding amount, but {{@endif}}another £200 charge will be added every seven days.

  @next -> @exit
:: story.rent.payment -> @exit
  @passage paid

  You hand Kim £200. {{npc.kim.subject | cap}} records the payment in the ledger.

  @if story.quest.rent.debt == 0
    @effect reminder clear rent_due
    "That clears the balance," Kim says. "The next weekly charge will still arrive on schedule."
  @else
    "Your outstanding balance is now £{{story.quest.rent.debt}}," Kim says.
  @endif

  @next -> @exit
  @#replace with kim sending you a threatening message if you don't pay your rent, when rent >= 1200
:: story.rent.debt-escalation -> @exit
  @pool interrupt
  @priority 200
  @when story.quest.rent.active
  @when story.quest.rent.debt >= 1200
  @when not flags.quest.rent.debt_escalation_seen
  @onenter
    @effect set flags.quest.rent.debt_escalation_seen
  @endonenter

  @passage warning

  A new message from Kim appears on your phone. The account has reached £{{story.quest.rent.debt}}, and {{npc.kim.subject}} is no longer willing to let it slide.

  [warning]This is a placeholder for the first overdue-rent consequence.[/warning]

  @next -> @exit
